---
// FaqAccordion.astro — renders Q&As AND emits FAQPage JSON-LD from the
// same data, so visible content and schema can't drift (Build Guide §4.5).
//
// BIDI ISOLATION (AR-2 B-15). An FAQ answer is prose that arrives as one opaque string, so
// until this component decomposed it there was nowhere to put isolation: `{a}` escapes, and
// a `<bdi>` written into frontmatter arrived as literal text. Gate 4n measured the cost on
// the first Arabic prose route, and E-1b measured a second defect no gate can see — the
// bare `$349` rendering as `349$`.
//
// `splitNamedRuns` says WHERE the site's own runs are; `<Bidi>` decides how isolation is
// expressed. Both halves already existed: B-2 §2.2 built `Bidi.astro` precisely so an
// `.astro` template would never reach for `set:html` to isolate a run, and this component
// had never called it.
//
// WHY ELEMENT NODES AND NOT `set:html`. Handing the formatter's string output to `set:html`
// would switch Astro's escaping off for the whole answer and oblige this file to switch it
// back on — a second definition of escaping to keep in step with Astro's own. Rendering an
// ARRAY instead keeps every text slice on Astro's normal interpolation path, so the escape
// is not preserved by care; it is never left. `set:html` appears nowhere below.
//
// WHY ALL NINE LOCALES AND NOT ONLY RTL ONES (owner decision, B-15 §8). `<bdi>` is a no-op
// in an LTR context — the property that made B-2 Phase B safe across eight locales. Making
// this path conditional on document direction would buy a few hundred bytes and cost the
// component its single invariant: FAQ text is rendered through `Bidi`, always, and there is
// one rendering path, one escaping model and one testing surface.
//
// BOTH FIELDS, NOT ONLY THE ANSWER. `q` renders in the same RTL paragraph context as `a`
// and can carry the same runs. Isolating one and not the other would reintroduce, inside
// this component, exactly the two-classes-of-prose split B-15 was raised to remove.
//
// `SchemaFaq` still receives the RAW strings. The isolation is a rendering concern; the
// JSON-LD carries the text, so §4.5's single source survives with nothing to strip.
import SchemaFaq from '../seo/SchemaFaq.astro';
import Bidi from '../Bidi.astro';
import { splitNamedRuns } from '../../lib/bidi-runs';

interface Props { faq: { q: string; a: string }[] }
const { faq } = Astro.props;
---
<div class="faq-accordion">
  {faq.map(({ q, a }, i) => (
    <details class="faq-item" name={`faq-${i}`}>
      <summary class="faq-question">{splitNamedRuns(q).map((p) => (p.run ? <Bidi>{p.text}</Bidi> : p.text))}</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">{splitNamedRuns(a).map((p) => (p.run ? <Bidi>{p.text}</Bidi> : p.text))}</div>
    </details>
  ))}
</div>
<SchemaFaq faq={faq} />

<style>
  .faq-item summary { cursor: pointer; }
  .faq-item summary:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--burnt-orange, #d4764e); outline-offset: 2px; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .faq-answer { transition: none; }
  }
</style>
